senses.gloss:
1. क्रुञ्च् (Pāṇ. iii, 2, 59) cl. 1. P. क्रुञ्चति, ‘to curve or make crooked’ or ‘to be crooked, move crookedly’, Dhātup. vii, 4;
 ‘to become small, shrink’, or ‘to make small, lessen’, ib.;
to go towards, approach, Vop.

क्रुड् cl. 6. P. क्रुडति, to sink, dive, Dhātup. xxviii, 100;
to be or become thick Comm. on VS. xxv, 8;
 (cf. क्रडन, √ कूड्, and क्रूड्) :
Caus. or cl. 10. P. fr. √ क्रूड्, क्रूदयति, to make thick (?), Kāṭh. vi, 3 and 7.

क्रुश् cl. 1. P. क्रो॑शति (rarely Ā., see क्रोशमान; aor. अ॑क्रुक्षत्, RV. x, 146, 4; perf. चुक्रोश, R.; fut. 2nd क्रोक्ष्यति and 1st क्रोष्टा, Pāṇ. vii, 2, 10; Siddh.),
to cry out, shriek, yell, bawl, call out, halloo, RV.; AV.; MBh. &c.;
to exclaim, R. i, 9, 59;
to lament, weep, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to make a singing noise (as the ear), Kauś. 58 :
Intens. चोक्रुशीति, Pāṇ. vii, 4, 82, Sch.;
